    \    Integral: 0\n    Unknown: 0\n    String: 599\n  isDataTypeInferred: false\n\
    \  histogram: null\n\n\nHere is the program:\nimport argparse\nimport os\nimport\
    \ re\nfrom datetime import date\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\n\
    \ndef slugify(text: str) -> str:\n    text = (text or \"\").lower()\n    text\
    \ = re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\", \"-\", text).strip(\"-\")\n    return text[:80]\n\n\
    \ndef to_cdn(url: str) -> str:\n    if not isinstance(url, str):\n        return\
    \ url\n    # Expecting Amazon media image URLs; convert size variant to a standard\
    \ UX342 size\n    try:\n        new_url = re.sub(r\"\\._V1_.+?\\.jpg\", \"._V1_UX342_.jpg\"\
    , url)\n        return new_url\n    except Exception:\n        return url\n\n\n\
    def main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    parser.add_argument('--input',\
    \ type=str, required=True)\n    parser.add_argument('--output', type=str, required=True)\n\
    \    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    input_file = os.path.join(args.input, 'new_data.csv')\n\
    \    os.makedirs(args.output, exist_ok=True)\n\n    df = pd.read_csv(input_file)\n\
    \n    # Basic type coercions needed by downstream logic\n    df['IMDB_Rating']\
    \ = pd.to_numeric(df['IMDB_Rating'], errors='coerce')\n    df['No_of_Votes'] =\
    \ pd.to_numeric(df['No_of_Votes'], errors='coerce').fillna(0).astype(int)\n  \
    \  df['Released_Year'] = pd.to_numeric(df['Released_Year'], errors='coerce').astype('Int64')\n\
    \    df['Meta_score'] = pd.to_numeric(df['Meta_score'], errors='coerce')\n   \
    \ current_year = date.today().year\n    df['RuntimeMinutes'] = df['Runtime'].astype(str).str.extract(r'(\\\
    d+)')[0].astype(int)\n\n    allowed_certificates = {\n        'U', 'UA', 'U/A',\
    \ 'A', 'G', 'PG', 'PG-13', 'R', 'NC-17', 'Not Rated', 'TV-14', 'TV-MA'\n    }\n\
    \    cert_canonical_map = {'U/A': 'UA'}\n    cert_norm = df['Certificate'].replace(cert_canonical_map)\n\
    \    cert_norm = cert_norm.where(cert_norm.isin({\n        'U', 'UA', 'A', 'G',\
    \ 'PG', 'PG-13', 'R', 'NC-17', 'Not Rated', 'TV-14', 'TV-MA'\n    }), other=np.nan)\n\
    \    df['CertificateNorm'] = cert_norm.fillna('Not Rated')\n    df['Poster_CDN']\
    \ = df['Poster_Link'].apply(to_cdn)\n\n    pairs = df[['IMDB_Rating', 'Meta_score']].dropna()\n\
    \    corr = pairs['IMDB_Rating'].corr(pairs['Meta_score']) if len(pairs) > 1 else\
    \ np.nan\n    meta_weight = 0.3 if (pd.notna(corr) and corr > 0.4) else 0.1\n\
    \    df['MetaNorm'] = df['Meta_score'] / 10.0\n    df['MetaNormFilled'] = df['MetaNorm'].fillna(df['IMDB_Rating'])\n\
    \    df['HybridRating'] = meta_weight * df['MetaNormFilled'] + (1.0 - meta_weight)\
    \ * df['IMDB_Rating']\n\n    m = df['No_of_Votes'].quantile(0.70)\n    C = df['HybridRating'].mean()\n\
    \    v = df['No_of_Votes']\n    R = df['HybridRating']\n    df['WeightedRank']\
    \ = (v / (v + m)) * R + (m / (v + m)) * C\n\n    filtered = df[(df['IMDB_Rating']\
    \ >= 7.0)].copy()\n\n    # Rank and pick top titles for the daily feed\n    top_n\
    \ = 200\n    today = date.today().isoformat()\n\n    filtered['catalog_id'] =\
    \ filtered.apply(lambda r: f\"{slugify(str(r['Series_Title']))}-{int(r['Released_Year'])}\"\
    ,\n                                            axis=1)\n\n    feed_cols = [\n\
    \        'catalog_id', 'Series_Title', 'Released_Year', 'Genre', 'IMDB_Rating',\
    \ 'Meta_score',\n        'No_of_Votes', 'RuntimeMinutes', 'CertificateNorm', 'Poster_CDN',\
    \ 'WeightedRank',\n        'Overview', 'Director', 'Star1', 'Star2', 'Star3',\
    \ 'Star4'\n    ]\n\n    available_cols = [c for c in feed_cols if c in filtered.columns]\n\
    \    top_feed = (\n        filtered.sort_values(['WeightedRank', 'No_of_Votes',\
    \ 'IMDB_Rating'], ascending=[False, False, False])\n        .head(top_n)[available_cols]\n\
    \        .copy()\n    )\n\n    top_feed.insert(0, 'feed_date', today)\n\n    output_file\
    \ = os.path.join(args.output, f'top_movies_catalog_{today}.csv')\n    top_feed.to_csv(output_file,\
    \ index=False)\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n\n\nFocus on the python\
    \ code for the Check object from pydeequ only. Generate a Python function\n`run_code()`\
    \ (taking no arguments) that returns a JSON object with a single key \"constraints\"\
    \nmapping to a list of objects, each with keys \"column_name\" and \"code_for_constraint\"\
    , where\n\"code_for_constraint\" is executable pydeequ Check code for that column.\
    \ Your code must not inspect\nany dataframe; only return the constraints.\n\n\
    Here is an example of the code to generate, please replace the example constraints\
    \ with the ones\nyou generate:\n\ndef run_code():\n    return {\n        \"constraints\"\
    : [\n            {\"column_name\": \"some_column\", \"code_for_constraint\": \"\
    .isComplete('some_column')\"},\n            {\"column_name\": \"another_column\"\
    , \"code_for_constraint\": \".isPositive('another_column')\"},\n        ]\n  \
    \  }\n\n\nOutput in this YAML format with reasoning:\n```yaml\nreasoning: |\n\
    \    The input parameters should be: param1 as a string, and param2 as a number.\n\
    \    To test the function, I will consider basic cases, edge cases, and corner\
    \ cases.\n    For this problem, I need to test...\ntest_cases:\n  - name: \"Basic\
    \ case\"\n    input: {param1: value1, param2: value2}\n    expected: result1\n\
    \  - name: \"Edge case - empty\"\n    input: {param1: value3, param2: value4}\n\
    \    expected: result2\n```"
  response: "```yaml\nreasoning: |\n  The dataset is consumed by a program that:\n\
    \    - Coerces numeric fields (IMDB_Rating, No_of_Votes, Released_Year, Meta_score),\n\
    \    - Parses Runtime into minutes by extracting digits,\n    - Normalizes Certificate\
    \ to a controlled set (defaulting others/missing to Not Rated),\n    - Converts\
    \ Poster_Link to a CDN variant but expects it to be a valid Amazon image URL,\n\
    \    - Computes derived fields and filters by IMDB_Rating >= 7.0,\n    - Builds\
    \ a catalog_id requiring a valid Released_Year and Series_Title.\n  From the profiling:\n\
    \    - IMDB_Rating, Released_Year, No_of_Votes, Poster_Link, Overview, Runtime,\
    \ Star1-4, Director, Series_Title, id are complete.\n    - IMDB_Rating is fractional,\
    \ within [0, 10] expected domain.\n    - No_of_Votes is integral and should be\
    \ non-negative.\n    - Released_Year is integral; assert a plausible year range.\n\
    \    - Runtime is a string like \"144 min\"; assert pattern.\n    - Poster_Link\
    \ is an Amazon image URL; assert pattern.\n    - Meta_score is ~85.6% complete;\
    \ assert minimum completeness.\n    - Certificate may be missing or outside the\
    \ allowed set; assert null or allowed list.\n  Therefore, the run_code() function\
    \ should return pydeequ Check constraints that:\n    - Ensure completeness and\
    \ uniqueness where needed (id),\n    - Enforce numeric domains and non-negativity\
    \ (IMDB_Rating, No_of_Votes),\n    - Enforce plausible temporal bounds (Released_Year),\n\
    \    - Validate formatting/patterns (Runtime, Poster_Link),\n    - Accommodate\
    \ partial completeness as profiled (Meta_score),\n    - Validate controlled vocab\
    \ with allowance for null (Certificate).\n  The following test cases validate\
    \ that the returned constraints include these critical checks without inspecting\
    \ any data.\ntest_cases:\n  - name: \"Structure: returns constraints list with\
    \ required keys\"\n    input: {}\n    expected:\n      must_have_top_level_key:\
    \ \"constraints\"\n      each_item_has_keys: [\"column_name\", \"code_for_constraint\"\
    ]\n      min_constraints_count: 10\n\n  - name: \"IMDB_Rating domain checks present\"\
    \n    input: {}\n    expected:\n      must_include:\n        - {column_name: \"\
    IMDB_Rating\", code_for_constraint: \".isComplete('IMDB_Rating')\"}\n        -\
    \ {column_name: \"IMDB_Rating\", code_for_constraint: \".isNonNegative('IMDB_Rating')\"\
    }\n        - {column_name: \"IMDB_Rating\", code_for_constraint: \".hasMax('IMDB_Rating',\
    \ lambda v: v <= 10.0)\"}\n\n  - name: \"No_of_Votes completeness and non-negativity\"\
    \n    input: {}\n    expected:\n      must_include:\n        - {column_name: \"\
    No_of_Votes\", code_for_constraint: \".isComplete('No_of_Votes')\"}\n        -\
    \ {column_name: \"No_of_Votes\", code_for_constraint: \".isNonNegative('No_of_Votes')\"\
    }\n\n  - name: \"Released_Year plausible range\"\n    input: {}\n    expected:\n\
    \      must_include:\n        - {column_name: \"Released_Year\", code_for_constraint:\
    \ \".hasMin('Released_Year', lambda v: v >= 1900)\"}\n        - {column_name:\
    \ \"Released_Year\", code_for_constraint: \".hasMax('Released_Year', lambda v:\
    \ v <= 2035)\"}\n\n  - name: \"Runtime formatting and completeness\"\n    input:\
    \ {}\n    expected:\n      must_include:\n        - {column_name: \"Runtime\"\
    , code_for_constraint: \".isComplete('Runtime')\"}\n        - {column_name: \"\
    Runtime\", code_for_constraint: \".containsPattern('Runtime', '^[0-9]+\\\\s*min$')\"\
    }\n\n  - name: \"Poster_Link is an Amazon image URL\"\n    input: {}\n    expected:\n\
    \      must_include:\n        - {column_name: \"Poster_Link\", code_for_constraint:\
    \ \".containsPattern('Poster_Link', '^https?://m\\\\.media-amazon\\\\.com/images/.+\\\
    \\.jpg$')\"}\n\n  - name: \"Certificate in allowed set or null; Meta_score completeness;\
    \ id uniqueness\"\n    input: {}\n    expected:\n      must_include:\n       \
    \ - {column_name: \"Certificate\", code_for_constraint: \".satisfies(\\\"Certificate\
    \ IS NULL OR Certificate IN ('U','UA','U/A','A','G','PG','PG-13','R','NC-17','Not\
    \ Rated','TV-14','TV-MA')\\\", 'Certificate_allowed', lambda v: v >= 1.0)\"}\n\
    \        - {column_name: \"Meta_score\", code_for_constraint: \".hasCompleteness('Meta_score',\
    \ lambda v: v >= 0.80)\"}\n        - {column_name: \"id\", code_for_constraint:\
    \ \".isComplete('id')\"}\n        - {column_name: \"id\", code_for_constraint:\
    \ \".isUnique('id')\"}\n```"
